okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Provider fallback: when the current provider answers 429 / a usage limit, serve the same request and the following ones from another provider whose credentials are already stored, return at the provider's reset time; CLI's own sign-in first when stored OAuth tokens are all limited; everything operable from the UI."
reported: "User, 2026-10-10 after the B2B diagnosis (../../diagnostics/oauth/b2b-all-tokens-limited.okf): '이런경우에 폴백으로 다른 프로바이더를에 설정되어있는 토큰이나 api값으로 실행할수있는방법 … 429가 발생했을때나 사용량이없을때 잠시 쿨다운을위해서 변경할수잇는방법 그리고 UI에서 최대한 편하게 제공해줄수있는 방법이 필요'. Choices: automatic + manual; return at the reset time; Claude Code and Codex; switch the same request immediately. Plan approved through the session's plan hook."
changes:
  core: "NEW provider_failover.py: settings/active/history in <workspace state>/provider-failover.json (config.json untouched); usable backups = stored API key (credentials.provider_config_api_keys) or Claude OAuth tokens for anthropic, client-local-auth providers excluded; cooldown from Retry-After or reset headers (else default_cooldown_minutes); on_rate_limited (only when nothing was written to the client, each provider once per request); effective() overlay with return only at a turn start; manual switch / return; maybe_fail_over helper; /fallback command parser; MCP handler."
  routing: "router_http._dispatch_with_failover wraps the runtime dispatch: overlay, FailoverRequested -> retry the pristine body on the backup (log provider_failover_route/retry). 429 points: claude_router native relay, openai_forwarding (stream before output / non-stream), openai_responses_router (generic, provider responses, codex-routed) incl. UpstreamFailure rate_limit; FailoverRequested re-raised past generic handlers."
  oauth: "oauth_token_pool.all_limited; OAuthRequestRun.cli_login_headers: when every stored token is limited the CLI's own sign-in (the headers it sent) is tried once, before provider fallback; limited tokens are not resent (setting cli_login_first, default on; injected by provider_failover to keep imports acyclic)."
  ui: "Menu 19 'Provider fallback [auto on · n/m backups ready · active …]' panel (provider_failover_menu.py): automatic on/off, CLI sign-in first, default cooldown, backups list (up/down/model/remove), add backup (providers with stored credentials), switch now (provider, model, minutes), return now, recent switches. Claude status line 'fallback <backup>/<model> until HH:MM (<provider> auto|manual)' with limits/context of the serving provider. /fallback slash command (status, PROVIDER [MINUTES] [MODEL], return, on|off) via router_shortcuts. Router MCP tool provider_fallback (status/switch/return/enable/disable). Event router.fallback."
  defaults: "Automatic fallback off until enabled; cli_login_first on."
tests: "NEW tests/test_provider_failover.py (13: usable backups, activation until Retry-After, default cooldown, disabled/started/non-429, backup also limited, turn-boundary return, manual switch/return, slash command, menu operations, cooldown validation, CLI sign-in first both paths); test_statusline +1 (fallback segment on a cp1252 stdout); MCP tool set, menu position pins and row 19 updated. Groups: unit 1796 OK, runtime 399 OK, router 1188 OK, channel 457 with the 2 known intermittent BoundaryScanDeadlineTests failures (also on committed HEAD). ruff clean; ciel_runtime.py 4980 lines; router 9611 200."
e2e:
  harness: "evidence/e2e_failover.py + e2e_failover_steps.py + console_driver.py. Stubs on 127.0.0.1: A for provider vllm (429 + Retry-After while armed), B for lm-studio (both answer /v1/messages in Anthropic form and chat completions). Isolated Ciel config/router/CODEX_HOME; menu in conhost driven by WriteConsoleInputW; Claude/Codex in Windows Terminal; turns via /ca/chat/notify; slash commands typed into the console."
  result: "Run 2026-10-10 02:07-02:10: menu enabled automatic fallback and added lm-studio (shots/03). Claude: TURN-1 got A's 429 once and the same turn was answered by B (screen 'STUB-B-REPLY-1'; log provider_failover_activated + retry); TURN-2 went straight to B; /fallback showed 'Active: lm-studio/stub-b-model until 02:08 (vllm auto)'; after the cooldown TURN-3 returned to A (provider_failover_returned why=cooldown over); /fallback lm-studio 5 -> TURN-4 on B; /fallback return -> TURN-5 on A. Codex (routed vllm): A's 429 -> same turn served by B (path /v1/responses)."
  statusline: "The E2E Claude used the user's ~/.claude, whose status line command is the installed Ciel script, so the status line was checked by rendering this commit's STATUSLINE_SCRIPT against the E2E state: '[ciel-runtime-vllm-stub-a-model] ws | fallback lm-studio/stub-b-model until 02:11 (vllm auto) | ctx est …' (e2e-1-failover/statusline-check.txt). That check found a crash: the first marker '⇄' cannot be printed on a cp1252 stdout; replaced by ASCII and covered by a test."
incidents:
  - "First runs: Claude in conhost and then with an isolated CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR never got channel input confirmed (channel_llm_inject_deferred / transcript_missing) - the known CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR receipt-lookup issue; the harness then let Claude use ~/.claude and run in Windows Terminal. One run had stub B answering chat-completions to lm-studio's /v1/messages ('malformed response' in Claude); the stub was fixed. Its scratch Claude project transcripts in ~/.claude/projects were removed afterwards."
not_verified:
  - "CLI-sign-in-first with real stored Claude OAuth tokens (needs a CLI OAuth login; unit-tested both paths)."
  - "Real Anthropic accepting a turn after other-provider turns (stub only; return happens only at a turn start)."
  - "/ca/manage/state exposure of the fallback state (not implemented; menu, /fallback, MCP and status line cover it)."
not_done: "Not committed, not pushed, not deployed; B2B session not changed."
